{
  "id": "COMPOUND:41549 - PROTEIN:6336",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Gelsemicine may influence Thrombopoietin through a series of target interactions. Gelsemicine is implicated in targeting SNU-387, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Neridienone A, Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, and Anolobine. All of these compounds are linked to Thrombopoietin, indicating a possible pathway where Gelsemicine may modulate Thrombopoietin through the activation or inhibition of SNU-387. The presence of multiple targets at the SNU-387 level suggests a possible role in the regulation of Thrombopoietin, potentially through the modulation of downstream signaling pathways. The cumulative evidence supports a mechanistic link between Gelsemicine and Thrombopoietin, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
